or live in rural areas.

284
00:10:22,893 --> 00:10:24,406
If you go over the limit,

285
00:10:24,406 --> 00:10:26,463
the extra charges can wipe out the

286
00:10:26,463 --> 00:10:28,581
savings of a lower monthly payment.

287
00:10:28,932 --> 00:10:31,253
Some leases let you buy extra miles

288
00:10:31,253 --> 00:10:32,115
at the start,

289
00:10:32,115 --> 00:10:34,105
at a lower price per mile than

290
00:10:34,105 --> 00:10:35,630
the penalty at the end.

291
00:10:35,810 --> 00:10:37,846
If you know you will drive more,

292
00:10:37,846 --> 00:10:39,882
buying miles up front can make a

293
00:10:39,882 --> 00:10:40,582
lease work.

294
00:10:40,762 --> 00:10:43,492
But it also raises the monthly payment,

295
00:10:43,492 --> 00:10:46,503
which reduces the main advantage of leasing

296
00:10:46,503 --> 00:10:47,833
in the first place.

297
00:10:48,013 --> 00:10:50,114
Always compare the final numbers.

298
00:10:50,464 --> 00:10:51,892
Here is the twist.

299
00:10:52,072 --> 00:10:54,649
Many people underestimate how much they drive.

300
00:10:54,829 --> 00:10:56,460
A family road trip,

301
00:10:56,460 --> 00:10:58,433
a new job farther away,

302
00:10:58,433 --> 00:11:00,836
or a summer of towing a boat

303
00:11:00,836 --> 00:11:03,153
can add thousands of miles.

304
00:11:03,333 --> 00:11:04,575
Before you lease,

305
00:11:04,575 --> 00:11:06,766
look at your last few years of

306
00:11:06,766 --> 00:11:09,833
driving, using old service records or your

307
00:11:09,833 --> 00:11:12,900
current odometer, and add a safety margin.

308
00:11:13,080 --> 00:11:15,663
Buying has no mileage penalty at all,

309
00:11:15,663 --> 00:11:18,734
although higher miles do lower resale value.

310
00:11:19,084 --> 00:11:22,044
Round five: modifications and wear.

311
00:11:22,224 --> 00:11:24,651
Truck owners love to customize.

312
00:11:24,831 --> 00:11:27,213
Lift kits, bigger tires,

313
00:11:27,213 --> 00:11:30,589
bed covers, racks and tow hitches.

314
00:11:30,769 --> 00:11:32,102
On a leased truck,

315
00:11:32,102 --> 00:11:35,211
many modifications are not allowed or must

316
00:11:35,211 --> 00:11:37,062
be removed before return.

317
00:11:37,242 --> 00:11:40,524
And trucks used for work get scratches,

318
00:11:40,524 --> 00:11:42,629
dents and worn interiors.

319
00:11:42,809 --> 00:11:45,185
A lease contract can charge you for

320
00:11:45,185 --> 00:11:47,697
wear beyond what it considers normal.

321
00:11:48,047 --> 00:11:50,252
Insurance is another detail.

322
00:11:50,432 --> 00:11:53,979
A leased vehicle usually requires higher coverage

323
00:11:53,979 --> 00:11:55,716
limits and gap coverage,

324
00:11:55,716 --> 00:11:58,176
because the lender owns the truck.

325
00:11:58,356 --> 00:12:01,321
That can raise your insurance bill compared

326
00:12:01,321 --> 00:12:03,321
with owning a truck outright,

327
00:12:03,321 --> 00:12:05,666
especially once a loan is paid off

328
00:12:05,666 --> 00:12:08,148
and you can choose your own coverage

329
00:12:08,148 --> 00:12:08,631
levels.

330
00:12:08,811 --> 00:12:11,830
Get insurance quotes for both options before

331
00:12:11,830 --> 00:12:12,584
you decide.

332
00:12:12,935 --> 00:12:14,924
This is why leasing is often a

333
00:12:14,924 --> 00:12:16,847
poor fit for a working truck.

334
00:12:17,027 --> 00:12:19,285
If your truck carries tools,

335
00:12:19,285 --> 00:12:21,542
lumber, gravel or equipment,

336
00:12:21,542 --> 00:12:22,832
it will show it.

337
00:12:23,012 --> 00:12:24,653
When you own the truck,

338
00:12:24,653 --> 00:12:26,437
wear only affects resale.

339
00:12:26,617 --> 00:12:27,762
When you lease it,

340
00:12:27,762 --> 00:12:29,606
wear can become a bill at the

341
00:12:29,606 --> 00:12:30,878
end of the contract.

342
00:12:31,058 --> 00:12:33,535
For a weekend truck that stays clean

343
00:12:33,535 --> 00:12:35,806
and stock, a lease is much safer.

344
00:12:36,157 --> 00:12:38,850
Round six: the end of the contract.

345
00:12:39,030 --> 00:12:40,324
When a lease ends,

346
00:12:40,324 --> 00:12:42,120
you can return the truck,

347
00:12:42,120 --> 00:12:43,845
buy it at a price set in

348
00:12:43,845 --> 00:12:46,217
the contract, or lease a new one.

349
00:12:46,397 --> 00:12:48,379
If the truck turns out to be

350
00:12:48,379 --> 00:12:50,927
worth more than the contract buyout,

351
00:12:50,927 --> 00:12:52,979
buying it can be a good deal.

352
00:12:53,159 --> 00:12:54,712
If it is worth less,

353
00:12:54,712 --> 00:12:57,351
you can simply hand back the keys.

354
00:12:57,531 --> 00:13:00,527
That flexibility is a real advantage of

355
00:13:00,527 --> 00:13:01,141
leasing.

356
00:13:01,492 --> 00:13:03,471
Here is the twist that has burned

357
00:13:03,471 --> 00:13:04,731
some buyers recently.

358
00:13:04,911 --> 00:13:08,138
When a model is discontinued or demand

359
00:13:08,138 --> 00:13:11,110
collapses, its value can drop fast.

360
00:13:11,290 --> 00:13:13,651
A leased truck protects you from that,

361
00:13:13,651 --> 00:13:16,074
because the risk belongs to the lender.

362
00:13:16,254 --> 00:13:17,809
A bought truck does not.

363
00:13:17,989 --> 00:13:20,469
If you are considering a truck whose

364
00:13:20,469 --> 00:13:21,847
future is uncertain,

365
00:13:21,847 --> 00:13:24,051
like a model with falling sales,

366
00:13:24,051 --> 00:13:26,669
leasing can shift the resale risk away

367
00:13:26,669 --> 00:13:27,289
from you.

368
00:13:27,639 --> 00:13:29,670
Look at the electric pickups.

369
00:13:29,850 --> 00:13:33,809
Ford ended the all-electric F-one-fifty Lightning in

370
00:13:33,809 --> 00:13:35,941
December twenty twenty-five,

371
00:13:35,941 --> 00:13:39,139
after a nineteen point five billion dollar

372
00:13:39,139 --> 00:13:41,727
charge, according to Fox Business.

373
00:13:41,907 --> 00:13:44,878
In the third quarter of twenty twenty-six,

374
00:13:44,878 --> 00:13:46,788
according to autoevolution,

375
00:13:46,788 --> 00:13:50,324
Ford sold just two hundred eighty-nine Lightnings.

376
00:13:50,504 --> 00:13:53,091
Many people who leased electric trucks could

377
00:13:53,091 --> 00:13:54,208
simply return them.

378
00:13:54,388 --> 00:13:56,749
Owners had to deal with the resale

379
00:13:56,749 --> 00:13:57,929
value themselves.

380
00:13:58,279 --> 00:14:01,159
Tariffs add another layer of uncertainty.

381
00:14:01,339 --> 00:14:04,458
In twenty twenty-five and twenty twenty-six,

382
00:14:04,458 --> 00:14:07,648
tariffs on imported vehicles and parts pushed

383
00:14:07,648 --> 00:14:08,711
some prices up.

384
00:14:08,891 --> 00:14:11,137
When new truck prices rise,

385
00:14:11,137 --> 00:14:13,882
used truck values often rise too,

386
00:14:13,882 --> 00:14:15,462
which helps owners.

387
00:14:15,642 --> 00:14:17,351
When prices fall,

388
00:14:17,351 --> 00:14:18,556
owners lose.

389
00:14:18,736 --> 00:14:20,795
A lease locks in the end value

390
00:14:20,795 --> 00:14:21,688
at the start,

391
00:14:21,688 --> 00:14:24,158
so you know exactly where you stand.

392
00:14:24,508 --> 00:14:26,030
On the other hand,

393
00:14:26,030 --> 00:14:29,241
trucks with strong resale reputations,

394
00:14:29,241 --> 00:14:31,185
like the Toyota Tacoma,

395
00:14:31,185 --> 00:14:32,368
reward owners.

396
00:14:32,548 --> 00:14:34,823
A truck that holds its value well

397
00:14:34,823 --> 00:14:37,511
builds equity, and that equity is yours

398
00:14:37,511 --> 00:14:39,096
when you sell or trade.

399
00:14:39,276 --> 00:14:40,238
With a lease,

400
00:14:40,238 --> 00:14:43,419
any value above the contract buyout belongs

401
00:14:43,419 --> 00:14:45,787
to the lender unless you buy the

402
00:14:45,787 --> 00:14:46,231
truck.

403
00:14:46,580 --> 00:14:48,033
Before the verdict,

404
00:14:48,033 --> 00:14:50,098
one more real-world factor:

405
00:14:50,098 --> 00:14:51,016
your credit.

406
00:14:51,196 --> 00:14:53,798
The best lease deals and the lowest

407
00:14:53,798 --> 00:14:56,401
loan rates go to buyers with strong

408
00:14:56,401 --> 00:14:57,442
credit scores.

409
00:14:57,622 --> 00:15:00,291
Buyers with weaker credit often see much

410
00:15:00,291 --> 00:15:03,026
higher rates, which can make both options

411
00:15:03,026 --> 00:15:03,694
expensive.

412
00:15:03,874 --> 00:15:06,601
Checking your credit before you visit the

413
00:15:06,601 --> 00:15:09,063
dealer, and getting a loan offer from

414
00:15:09,063 --> 00:15:10,992
a bank or credit union first,

415
00:15:10,992 --> 00:15:13,453
gives you a number to compare against

416
00:15:13,453 --> 00:15:14,717
the dealer's offer.

417
00:15:15,067 --> 00:15:17,796
And never negotiate only the monthly payment.

418
00:15:17,976 --> 00:15:20,606
A dealer can hit almost any monthly

419
00:15:20,606 --> 00:15:23,235
number by changing the loan length,

420
00:15:23,235 --> 00:15:25,940
the down payment or the lease terms.

421
00:15:26,120 --> 00:15:28,931
Negotiate the price of the truck first,

422
00:15:28,931 --> 00:15:30,300
then the financing.

423
00:15:30,480 --> 00:15:32,883
That one habit protects you whether you

424
00:15:32,883 --> 00:15:33,684
lease or buy.

425
00:15:34,034 --> 00:15:36,316
There is one more cost that many

426
00:15:36,316 --> 00:15:38,597
people forget: the down payment.

427
00:15:38,777 --> 00:15:41,240
A large down payment on a lease

428
00:15:41,240 --> 00:15:42,829
is especially risky.

429
00:15:43,009 --> 00:15:45,438
If the truck is stolen or totaled

430
00:15:45,438 --> 00:15:46,837
early in the lease,

431
00:15:46,837 --> 00:15:49,634
the insurance and gap coverage pay off

432
00:15:49,634 --> 00:15:52,211
the lease, but your down payment is

433
00:15:52,211 --> 00:15:53,168
usually gone.

434
00:15:53,348 --> 00:15:56,450
Many experts suggest putting as little money

435
00:15:56,450 --> 00:15:58,636
down on a lease as possible for

436
00:15:58,636 --> 00:16:00,047
exactly that reason.

437
00:16:00,396 --> 00:16:01,428
With a purchase,

438
00:16:01,428 --> 00:16:03,554
a down payment works differently.

439
00:16:03,734 --> 00:16:05,144
It reduces the loan,

440
00:16:05,144 --> 00:16:07,894
lowers the total interest and helps you

441
00:16:07,894 --> 00:16:09,586
avoid being upside down.

442
00:16:09,766 --> 00:16:11,913
That money becomes equity in a truck

443
00:16:11,913 --> 00:16:12,390
you own.

444
00:16:12,570 --> 00:16:15,083
So the same five thousand dollars can

445
00:16:15,083 --> 00:16:17,256
be smart on a purchase and risky

446
00:16:17,256 --> 00:16:18,003
on a lease.

447
00:16:18,183 --> 00:16:20,231
It all depends on which path you

448
00:16:20,231 --> 00:16:20,679
choose.

449
00:16:21,029 --> 00:16:22,993
And think about how your life might

450
00:16:22,993 --> 00:16:23,386
change.

451
00:16:23,566 --> 00:16:24,397
A new job,

452
00:16:24,397 --> 00:16:26,805
a move, a growing family or a

453
00:16:26,805 --> 00:16:30,045
business can change the truck you need.

454
00:16:30,225 --> 00:16:32,421
A lease locks you into a fixed

455
00:16:32,421 --> 00:16:34,764
term, and ending it early can be

456
00:16:34,764 --> 00:16:35,496
expensive.

457
00:16:35,676 --> 00:16:37,784
A purchased truck can be sold at

458
00:16:37,784 --> 00:16:40,419
any time, although you take whatever the

459
00:16:40,419 --> 00:16:41,341
market offers.

460
00:16:41,521 --> 00:16:43,832
Flexibility has value too.

461
00:16:44,181 --> 00:16:46,007
So who should lease a truck in

462
00:16:46,007 --> 00:16:47,223
twenty twenty-seven?

463
00:16:47,403 --> 00:16:49,932
Someone who drives a predictable,

464
00:16:49,932 --> 00:16:51,848
moderate number of miles,

465
00:16:51,848 --> 00:16:54,301
keeps the truck clean and stock,

466
00:16:54,301 --> 00:16:56,906
wants a new truck every few years,

467
00:16:56,906 --> 00:16:59,359
and is not eligible for the loan

468
00:16:59,359 --> 00:17:02,577
interest deduction, or is choosing a truck

469
00:17:02,577 --> 00:17:04,493
not assembled in America.

470
00:17:04,673 --> 00:17:06,882
Leasing can also make sense for a

471
00:17:06,882 --> 00:17:08,957
model with an uncertain future.

472
00:17:09,307 --> 00:17:10,689
And who should buy?

473
00:17:10,869 --> 00:17:13,819
Someone who keeps trucks for many years,

474
00:17:13,819 --> 00:17:15,441
drives a lot of miles,

475
00:17:15,441 --> 00:17:17,432
tows, works the truck hard,

476
00:17:17,432 --> 00:17:19,054
or likes to modify it.

477
00:17:19,234 --> 00:17:22,054
Buying also gets the edge in twenty

478
00:17:22,054 --> 00:17:25,115
twenty-six for eligible buyers of new,

479
00:17:25,115 --> 00:17:26,807
U S assembled trucks,

480
00:17:26,807 --> 00:17:29,869
thanks to the loan interest deduction.

481
00:17:30,049 --> 00:17:32,376
For most traditional truck owners,

482
00:17:32,376 --> 00:17:35,320
buying remains the better long-term choice.

483
00:17:35,669 --> 00:17:37,841
There is also a middle path.

484
00:17:38,021 --> 00:17:40,719
Some buyers finance a truck with a

485
00:17:40,719 --> 00:17:43,735
shorter loan, like four or five years,

486
00:17:43,735 --> 00:17:45,799
and a bigger down payment.

487
00:17:45,979 --> 00:17:48,044
That reduces total interest,

488
00:17:48,044 --> 00:17:49,888
avoids being upside down,

489
00:17:49,888 --> 00:17:53,281
and still qualifies for the interest deduction

490
00:17:53,281 --> 00:17:55,568
if the truck and buyer meet the

491
00:17:55,568 --> 00:17:56,010
rules.

492
00:17:56,190 --> 00:17:58,262
It is less exciting than a low

493
00:17:58,262 --> 00:18:00,610
lease payment, but it is often the

494
00:18:00,610 --> 00:18:02,820
cheapest path to owning a truck.

495
00:18:03,169 --> 00:18:05,201
And here is the final twist.

496
00:18:05,381 --> 00:18:07,865
The worst choice is not leasing or

497
00:18:07,865 --> 00:18:08,377
buying.

498
00:18:08,557 --> 00:18:11,062
It is stretching a loan to eighty-four

499
00:18:11,062 --> 00:18:13,172
months to afford a truck that is

500
00:18:13,172 --> 00:18:14,095
too expensive.

501
00:18:14,275 --> 00:18:15,657
According to Edmunds,

502
00:18:15,657 --> 00:18:18,488
twenty-one point two percent of new vehicle

503
00:18:18,488 --> 00:18:21,385
buyers who financed were paying one thousand

504
00:18:21,385 --> 00:18:23,360
dollars or more a month in the

505
00:18:23,360 --> 00:18:25,664
third quarter of twenty twenty-six.

506
00:18:25,844 --> 00:18:28,324
If the payment only works with a

507
00:18:28,324 --> 00:18:31,578
seven-year loan, the truck may simply cost

508
00:18:31,578 --> 00:18:32,276
too much.

509
00:18:32,625 --> 00:18:35,760
One last consideration is the truck's warranty.

510
00:18:35,940 --> 00:18:39,419
Most leases end before the factory warranty

511
00:18:39,419 --> 00:18:42,250
runs out, so lessees rarely pay for

512
00:18:42,250 --> 00:18:43,382
major repairs.

513
00:18:43,562 --> 00:18:45,995
Owners who keep trucks for many years

514
00:18:45,995 --> 00:18:48,821
will eventually pay for repairs themselves.

515
00:18:49,001 --> 00:18:50,815
That is part of the cost of

516
00:18:50,815 --> 00:18:53,300
owning, and it is why reliability and

517
00:18:53,300 --> 00:18:56,053
a good maintenance history matter so much

518
00:18:56,053 --> 00:18:56,792
if you buy.

519
00:18:57,141 --> 00:18:59,107
If you buy and plan to keep

520
00:18:59,107 --> 00:19:00,564
the truck long term,

521
00:19:00,564 --> 00:19:03,258
set aside money each month for future

522
00:19:03,258 --> 00:19:05,005
maintenance and repairs,

523
00:19:05,005 --> 00:19:07,117
as if you were still making a

524
00:19:07,117 --> 00:19:08,136
small payment.

525
00:19:08,316 --> 00:19:10,516
When the big repair bill arrives,

526
00:19:10,516 --> 00:19:12,182
it will not hurt as much.

527
00:19:12,362 --> 00:19:15,458
That simple habit turns the payment-free years

528
00:19:15,458 --> 00:19:16,670
into real savings.

529
00:19:17,019 --> 00:19:19,440
So here is your checklist before you

530
00:19:19,440 --> 00:19:19,910
decide.

531
00:19:20,090 --> 00:19:22,585
First, compare the total cost of both

532
00:19:22,585 --> 00:19:24,810
options over the time you plan to

533
00:19:24,810 --> 00:19:25,821
keep the truck,

534
00:19:25,821 --> 00:19:27,776
not just the monthly payment.

535
00:19:27,956 --> 00:19:30,905
Second, check your real yearly mileage.

536
00:19:31,085 --> 00:19:34,182
Third, check whether the truck is assembled

537
00:19:34,182 --> 00:19:36,054
in the U S and whether you

538
00:19:36,054 --> 00:19:38,575
qualify for the interest deduction,

539
00:19:38,575 --> 00:19:40,303
with a tax professional.

540
00:19:40,654 --> 00:19:43,336
Fourth, think about how you use the

541
00:19:43,336 --> 00:19:46,862
truck: work, towing and modifications point to

542
00:19:46,862 --> 00:19:47,399
buying.

543
00:19:47,579 --> 00:19:50,001
And fifth, read the end of the

544
00:19:50,001 --> 00:19:52,019
lease contract carefully:

545
00:19:52,019 --> 00:19:53,391
the buyout price,

546
00:19:53,391 --> 00:19:54,683
the mileage fee,

547
00:19:54,683 --> 00:19:56,217
and the wear rules.

548
00:19:56,397 --> 00:19:59,408
Those three lines decide whether a lease

549
00:19:59,408 --> 00:20:00,913
is a deal or a trap.

550
00:20:01,262 --> 00:20:03,336
We put all of these checks into

551
00:20:03,336 --> 00:20:06,278
the Twenty Twenty-Seven Truck Buyer's Guide,

552
00:20:06,278 --> 00:20:08,753
with the questions to ask the finance

553
00:20:08,753 --> 00:20:11,026
office and the numbers to compare.

554
00:20:11,206 --> 00:20:13,335
The link is in the description and

555
00:20:13,335 --> 00:20:14,713
in the pinned comment.

556
00:20:14,893 --> 00:20:16,775
Subscribe for the next video,

557
00:20:16,775 --> 00:20:19,242
about seven dealer tricks to watch for

558
00:20:19,242 --> 00:20:20,605
when you buy a truck.

559
00:20:20,785 --> 00:20:21,865
Thanks for watching.
